				</p>

				<h3 class="cas-sub">Topic-specialist drafters — a tested dead end</h3>
				<p>
					Five draft models scored across four topics, each against the same target output. Same-size code
					specialists merely <strong>tie</strong> the generalist on code; the math specialist is
					<strong> worse</strong> than the generalist even on math. The best possible router would pick
					the general 1.5B everywhere. Acceptance is about matching the <em>target's own style</em>, and a
					same-family generalist matches a generalist target better than a narrow expert does.
					<strong> Bigger helps; specializing doesn't.</strong>
